---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { allQuestions, allPapers } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About this site" context="about" description="Who runs alevelenvironmentalsciencetutor.com and where the questions, mark schemes and ratings come from.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p>alevelenvironmentalsciencetutor.com is run by {site.company}, an A-level tutoring business with a small team of specialist tutors. The site exists to give AQA Environmental Science students the past-paper material they actually use, sorted the way they revise, free and without sign-up; and to introduce students who want more help to a specialist tutor.</p>
  <h2>Where the material comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Questions, mark schemes and examiner comments</strong> are from AQA's own published papers for A-level Environmental Science (7447): the specimen papers, November 2020, November 2021 and June 2022 to June 2025: {allPapers.length} papers and {allQuestions.length.toLocaleString()} question parts. Each part has been tagged to the specification statements it assesses, its maths and practical skills and its question type. The figure, table or passage a question is built on is shown above each of its parts.</li>
    <li><strong>What is missing.</strong> The June 2019 papers are no longer on AQA's public site, and the June 2026 papers are not yet public. AQA published no examiners' reports for the November 2020 and November 2021 series. Where AQA has removed a third-party photograph or extract for copyright reasons, the gap is AQA's.</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty ratings</strong> (Easy, Medium and Hard) come from the wording and figures of AQA's examiners' reports for June 2022 to June 2025. Parts the report says nothing clear about are left unrated.</li>
    <li><strong>Key-term cards and the notes on research methods, maths skills, essays and nine-mark questions</strong> are the site's own writing, being checked by our tutor; they are not copied from AQA's material.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade boundaries and exam dates</strong> are AQA's published figures.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>The tutoring is by Oliver, who has examined AQA Environmental Science for five years and teaches it at a top sixth-form college; see the <a href="/tutors/">tutor page</a>. The site is built and maintained by the same small team that runs <a href="https://www.alevelbiologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelbiologytutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.alevelgeographytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelgeographytutor.com</a> and <a href="https://www.chemistryaleveltutor.com" rel="noopener">chemistryaleveltutor.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>If you find one, tell us on the <a href="/report/">report a mistake</a> page; corrections usually go live the same week.</p>
</Base>
